WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:07.359
The Walking Dead is one of the most popular
shows on television, yet some of its stars

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:09.070
are still mostly unknown.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.920
For instance, consider Lauren Cohan.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.860
She's played Maggie for five seasons, but
how much do you really know about her?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.400
Here are some fun things that most fans of
The Walking Dead probably don't know about

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.700
the career of one of the show's toughest survivors.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.090
She grew up in the UK

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:26.160
If you've heard Lauren Cohan speak out of
character, it's probably a bit jarring to

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.090
discover she has an English accent.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.270
So what gives?

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.410
Turns out that Cohan's mother is English.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.410
Mystery solved!

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.539
“I was born in New Jersey, my mom is English
my dad is American and I move to England so

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:43.210
I have a bit of a, a bit of a the both sides
of the pond…”

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.980
Supernatural Star

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.270
Cohan got her big break in 2005 with a role
in the film Casanova, then followed it up

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.460
the next year with a role in Van Wilder: The
Rise of Taj.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.219
But it was her turn as Bela Talbot on Supernatural
that first brought her to the widespread attention

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:57.690
of television fans.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.710
Unfortunately, that attention was...less than
positive.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.710
An anti-hero who stole magical artifacts and
sold them to the highest bidder, Bela proved

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.950
to be wildly unpopular with fans.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.430
After just six episodes, she was killed off.

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:15.290
It just proves that fans are even deadlier
than zombies.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.820
Moment of Immortality

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:19.930
It's no surprise that the producers of The
Walking Dead approached Lauren for the role

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:24.360
of Maggie given that she already had a reputation
in the industry for playing strong women on

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.490
horror shows.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:30.000
Case in point: after ending her run on Supernatural,
Cohan landed a recurring role on The Vampire

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.590
Diaries as Rose, an immortal vampire.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.950
Sadly, immortality isn't quite what it used
to be, and after six episodes she was staked

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.110
through the heart.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:42.320
“One, Two”

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.020
Alas!

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.740
Bad Luck for Chuck

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:50.860
In 2011, Cohan took a break from the world
of television horror and instead became a

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.850
villainous superspy on Chuck.

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.720
In the role of Vivian McArthur Volkoff, Cohan
went full-on evil, hiring hitmen to assassinate

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.020
Zachary Levi's lead character and even attempting
to murder his fiancée out of revenge.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.440
“Ok you don’t do things like this.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.630
Please don’t do this.”

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.580
“I already have.”

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.970
That doesn't sound like sweet Maggie at all!

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.180
Commitment Issues

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.560
Fun fact: Cohan almost missed out on The Walking
Dead because she was under contract to a different

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.560
show.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.590
Back in 2011, Cohan filmed a pilot for The
CW called Heavenly, in which she played a

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:25.740
lawyer who teamed up with an angel to… fight
crime or something?

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.750
Fellow CW stars Ben Aldridge and Ryan Eggold
were also cast, but despite the network nepotism,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.880
The CW passed on Heavenly, freeing her up
to do The Walking Dead instead.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.100
“Yeah, Woooo, Yeah, Wooo, Yeah”

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.100
Horror Hater

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.280
Perhaps the craziest thing about Cohan's career?

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.890
Even though all of her most famous roles have
come in horror stories, including her part

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.610
in the feature film The Boy, she isn't actually
much of a fan of the genre.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.700
In fact, she told Media Blvd.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.290
Magazine that it scares her to death:

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.390
"I have a very weak stomach for horror.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.630
It's great, but it's something that you want
to watch with a girlfriend or a friend because

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.790
you can scream with somebody else."

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:05.100
You don't have to tell that to Walking Dead
fans.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.750
They already know.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.740
“Neighbors heard screaming and gunshots
coming from a family's home so officers raced

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:16.370
to the scene and Mass, turns out the family
was watching The Walking Dead”

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.350
Thanks for watching!

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.680
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.030
And leave us a comment to let us know which
of Lauren's TV roles is your favorite…

